<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marius (emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 269</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Marcus Aurelius Marius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marius was a Roman usurper who ruled the breakaway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallic-empire">Gallic Empire</a> briefly in 269, after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/postumus">Postumus</a> by his troops. According to later Roman sources he had been a blacksmith before rising in the army. He was killed after a reign of only a few weeks or months, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victorinus">Victorinus</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marius-emperor.jpg" alt="Marius (emperor)" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Tyrex rean at Turkish Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marius4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
